not the starting number.

860
00:27:49,534 --> 00:27:50,625
Objection two.

861
00:27:50,805 --> 00:27:52,330
The market is too high,

862
00:27:52,330 --> 00:27:53,789
I'll wait for a crash.

863
00:27:53,969 --> 00:27:56,558
Nobody can reliably predict crashes.

864
00:27:56,738 --> 00:27:58,682
People who wait often miss years of

865
00:27:58,682 --> 00:27:59,071
growth.

866
00:27:59,251 --> 00:28:00,591
Investing every month,

867
00:28:00,591 --> 00:28:02,053
in good markets and bad,

868
00:28:02,053 --> 00:28:04,063
means you buy some shares at high

869
00:28:04,063 --> 00:28:05,890
prices and some at low prices,

870
00:28:05,890 --> 00:28:07,413
without needing to guess.

871
00:28:07,763 --> 00:28:09,051
Objection three.

872
00:28:09,231 --> 00:28:11,402
Social Security won't be there for me.

873
00:28:11,582 --> 00:28:15,193
According to the Social Security Trustees reports,

874
00:28:15,193 --> 00:28:18,226
the program's trust funds are projected to

875
00:28:18,226 --> 00:28:20,754
be depleted in the 2030s if nothing

876
00:28:20,754 --> 00:28:22,415
changes, but even then,

877
00:28:22,415 --> 00:28:25,592
ongoing payroll taxes are projected to cover

878
00:28:25,592 --> 00:28:27,325
most scheduled benefits.

879
00:28:27,505 --> 00:28:30,670
Many experts expect changes to the program,

880
00:28:30,670 --> 00:28:32,289
not its disappearance.

881
00:28:32,469 --> 00:28:34,478
Still, it's wise to plan with a

882
00:28:34,478 --> 00:28:35,580
margin of safety.

883
00:28:35,931 --> 00:28:37,045
Objection four.

884
00:28:37,225 --> 00:28:38,990
I'd rather enjoy life now.

885
00:28:39,170 --> 00:28:39,994
Me too.

886
00:28:40,174 --> 00:28:42,682
A good plan includes real fun money.

887
00:28:42,862 --> 00:28:45,219
The point isn't to sacrifice your thirties.

888
00:28:45,399 --> 00:28:47,484
It's to make sure your fifties and

889
00:28:47,484 --> 00:28:49,079
sixties are enjoyable too.

890
00:28:49,259 --> 00:28:50,655
With a balanced budget,

891
00:28:50,655 --> 00:28:52,173
you don't have to choose.

892
00:28:52,524 --> 00:28:53,719
And objection five.

893
00:28:53,899 --> 00:28:55,084
I'll just work longer.

894
00:28:55,264 --> 00:28:57,098
Working longer can help,

895
00:28:57,098 --> 00:28:59,316
but it isn't always a choice.

896
00:28:59,496 --> 00:29:02,530
Health problems, caregiving and layoffs can force

897
00:29:02,530 --> 00:29:04,511
earlier retirement than planned.

898
00:29:04,691 --> 00:29:07,219
Many surveys of retirees find a large

899
00:29:07,219 --> 00:29:10,020
share retired earlier than they expected.

900
00:29:10,200 --> 00:29:12,457
Saving now gives you options if life

901
00:29:12,457 --> 00:29:13,648
changes your plans.

902
00:29:13,998 --> 00:29:15,754
Let me answer the questions I hear

903
00:29:15,754 --> 00:29:17,562
most from people in their thirties.

904
00:29:17,912 --> 00:29:18,759
Question one.

905
00:29:18,939 --> 00:29:20,342
Is it too late to start at

906
00:29:20,342 --> 00:29:21,853
thirty eight or thirty nine?

907
00:29:22,033 --> 00:29:22,300
No.

908
00:29:22,480 --> 00:29:24,587
You still have more than twenty five

909
00:29:24,587 --> 00:29:26,811
years before a typical retirement age.

910
00:29:26,991 --> 00:29:29,946
Saving fifteen to twenty percent and staying

911
00:29:29,946 --> 00:29:32,633
consistent can build a solid retirement.

912
00:29:32,813 --> 00:29:36,041
And catch up contributions become available at

913
00:29:36,041 --> 00:29:37,585
fifty under IRS rules.

914
00:29:37,935 --> 00:29:38,887
Question two.

915
00:29:39,067 --> 00:29:41,390
Should I pay off my mortgage early

916
00:29:41,390 --> 00:29:42,074
or invest?

917
00:29:42,254 --> 00:29:43,994
It depends on your rate and your

918
00:29:43,994 --> 00:29:44,320
goals.

919
00:29:44,500 --> 00:29:47,154
Many people with low rate mortgages choose

920
00:29:47,154 --> 00:29:48,292
to invest instead,

921
00:29:48,292 --> 00:29:51,451
because long term market returns have historically

922
00:29:51,451 --> 00:29:52,209
been higher.

923
00:29:52,389 --> 00:29:54,571
Others value the peace of mind of

924
00:29:54,571 --> 00:29:55,628
a paid off home.

925
00:29:55,808 --> 00:29:58,104
Either can be reasonable once your retirement

926
00:29:58,104 --> 00:29:59,175
savings are on track.

927
00:29:59,526 --> 00:30:00,605
Question three.

928
00:30:00,785 --> 00:30:03,123
My partner and I have very different

929
00:30:03,123 --> 00:30:03,966
money styles.

930
00:30:04,146 --> 00:30:05,052
What do we do?

931
00:30:05,232 --> 00:30:06,231
That's very common.

932
00:30:06,411 --> 00:30:09,309
Start with shared goals rather than spending

933
00:30:09,309 --> 00:30:09,835
details.

934
00:30:10,015 --> 00:30:12,230
Agree on savings targets together,

935
00:30:12,230 --> 00:30:15,097
then give each person some personal spending

936
00:30:15,097 --> 00:30:17,051
money with no questions asked.

937
00:30:17,231 --> 00:30:19,891
That reduces conflict while keeping the plan

938
00:30:19,891 --> 00:30:20,435
on track.

939
00:30:20,786 --> 00:30:21,714
Question four.

940
00:30:21,894 --> 00:30:24,298
Should I take money out of my

941
00:30:24,298 --> 00:30:26,039
401k to pay off debt?

942
00:30:26,219 --> 00:30:28,274
Usually, it's best to avoid it.

943
00:30:28,454 --> 00:30:31,813
Early withdrawals can trigger taxes and penalties,

944
00:30:31,813 --> 00:30:34,097
and you lose years of compounding.

945
00:30:34,277 --> 00:30:36,573
Loans from a 401k have their own

946
00:30:36,573 --> 00:30:39,443
risks, especially if you leave your job.

947
00:30:39,623 --> 00:30:41,620
Explore other options first.

948
00:30:41,970 --> 00:30:43,235
And question five.

949
00:30:43,415 --> 00:30:45,635
How do I stop feeling anxious about

950
00:30:45,635 --> 00:30:46,016
money?

951
00:30:46,196 --> 00:30:47,833
Action helps more than worry.

952
00:30:48,013 --> 00:30:49,196
Make a written plan,

953
00:30:49,196 --> 00:30:50,852
automate as much as you can,

954
00:30:50,852 --> 00:30:52,982
and review once a quarter instead of

955
00:30:52,982 --> 00:30:53,574
every day.

956
00:30:53,754 --> 00:30:56,585
As your emergency fund grows and your

957
00:30:56,585 --> 00:30:57,810
net worth rises,

958
00:30:57,810 --> 00:31:00,488
many people find the anxiety fades.

959
00:31:00,838 --> 00:31:01,975
Question six.

960
00:31:02,155 --> 00:31:04,396
Should I hire a financial advisor?

961
00:31:04,576 --> 00:31:05,545
It can help,

962
00:31:05,545 --> 00:31:08,291
especially for complex situations.

963
00:31:08,471 --> 00:31:09,096
If you do,

964
00:31:09,096 --> 00:31:10,971
look for a fee only fiduciary,

965
00:31:10,971 --> 00:31:13,409
someone legally required to act in your

966
00:31:13,409 --> 00:31:16,472
best interest, and understand exactly how they're

967
00:31:16,472 --> 00:31:16,784
paid.

968
00:31:16,964 --> 00:31:19,476
For many people with simple situations,

969
00:31:19,476 --> 00:31:21,731
a target date fund and an automated

970
00:31:21,731 --> 00:31:22,955
plan work well too.

971
00:31:23,305 --> 00:31:24,640
And question seven.

972
00:31:24,820 --> 00:31:26,729
What's the single most important move in

973
00:31:26,729 --> 00:31:27,397
your thirties?

974
00:31:27,577 --> 00:31:30,097
Raising your savings rate and automating it.

975
00:31:30,277 --> 00:31:31,621
Everything else helps,

976
00:31:31,621 --> 00:31:33,455
but nothing replaces a steady,

977
00:31:33,455 --> 00:31:36,021
automatic share of every paycheck going to

978
00:31:36,021 --> 00:31:36,755
your future.

979
00:31:37,105 --> 00:31:37,999
Question eight.

980
00:31:38,179 --> 00:31:39,920
How much should I keep in cash

981
00:31:39,920 --> 00:31:41,023
versus investments?

982
00:31:41,203 --> 00:31:43,272
A common approach is to keep your

983
00:31:43,272 --> 00:31:45,780
emergency fund and any money you'll need

984
00:31:45,780 --> 00:31:47,410
within the next few years,

985
00:31:47,410 --> 00:31:48,664
like a down payment,

986
00:31:48,664 --> 00:31:50,983
in high yield savings or similar safe

987
00:31:50,983 --> 00:31:51,547
accounts.

988
00:31:51,727 --> 00:31:54,077
Money for goals ten or more years

989
00:31:54,077 --> 00:31:55,644
away, like retirement,

990
00:31:55,644 --> 00:31:58,136
can usually be invested for growth.

991
00:31:58,316 --> 00:32:00,794
Matching the account to the timeline reduces

992
00:32:00,794 --> 00:32:03,159
the chance you'll have to sell investments

993
00:32:03,159 --> 00:32:03,947
at a bad time.

994
00:32:04,297 --> 00:32:06,398
And one last thought before the recap.

995
00:32:06,578 --> 00:32:08,520
Feeling behind is a feeling,

996
00:32:08,520 --> 00:32:09,283
not a fact.

997
00:32:09,463 --> 00:32:11,422
The fact is that you have time,

998
00:32:11,422 --> 00:32:14,202
income, and better tools than any generation

999
00:32:14,202 --> 00:32:14,897
before you.

1000
00:32:15,077 --> 00:32:16,786
What you do with the next five

1001
00:32:16,786 --> 00:32:19,122
years matters far more than what happened

1002
00:32:19,122 --> 00:32:20,034
in the last ten.

1003
00:32:20,214 --> 00:32:21,317
Start this week.

1004
00:32:21,667 --> 00:32:22,537
Quick recap.

1005
00:32:22,717 --> 00:32:25,175
Starting at thirty five with five hundred

1006
00:32:25,175 --> 00:32:27,454
dollars a month could build around six

1007
00:32:27,454 --> 00:32:30,032
hundred ten thousand dollars by sixty five.

1008
00:32:30,212 --> 00:32:32,175
Raising that to one thousand a month

1009
00:32:32,175 --> 00:32:33,648
could build over a million.

1010
00:32:33,828 --> 00:32:34,757
Don't panic.

1011
00:32:34,937 --> 00:32:37,956
Don't freeze, gamble or over restrict.

1012
00:32:38,306 --> 00:32:39,896
The fifteen moves.

1013
00:32:40,076 --> 00:32:41,377
Get your full picture.

1014
00:32:41,557 --> 00:32:43,507
Build a real emergency fund.

1015
00:32:43,687 --> 00:32:45,092
Clear high interest debt.

1016
00:32:45,272 --> 00:32:47,954
Raise your savings rate to fifteen percent

1017
00:32:47,954 --> 00:32:48,465
or more.

1018
00:32:48,645 --> 00:32:50,607
Use tax advantaged accounts.

1019
00:32:50,787 --> 00:32:51,924
Grow your income.

1020
00:32:52,104 --> 00:32:53,799
Control the big three.

1021
00:32:53,979 --> 00:32:55,524
Buy a home only when ready.

1022
00:32:55,874 --> 00:32:57,104
Protect your family.

1023
00:32:57,284 --> 00:32:59,119
Put retirement before college.

1024
00:32:59,299 --> 00:33:00,783
Get on the same page with your

1025
00:33:00,783 --> 00:33:01,179
partner.

1026
00:33:01,359 --> 00:33:03,867
Invest simply and stay invested.

1027
00:33:04,047 --> 00:33:06,056
Use windfalls on purpose.

1028
00:33:06,236 --> 00:33:08,070
Avoid lifestyle creep.

1029
00:33:08,250 --> 00:33:09,667
And review once a quarter.

1030
00:33:10,017 --> 00:33:11,677
This week, do move one.

1031
00:33:11,857 --> 00:33:13,970
One honest hour with your numbers.

1032
00:33:14,150 --> 00:33:16,164
Then pick the next move and keep

1033
00:33:16,164 --> 00:33:16,541
going.

1034
00:33:16,721 --> 00:33:18,462
If you want to go further,

1035
00:33:18,462 --> 00:33:20,805
watch my video on retiring early on

1036
00:33:20,805 --> 00:33:21,876
a normal income.

1037
00:33:22,056 --> 00:33:23,299
I'm Ryan Rover.

1038
00:33:23,479 --> 00:33:24,628
See you in the next one.
